### Various system- or environment-specific tweakable parameters.

## Settings for Solaris 2.x systems

## NOTES:
##
## This definition was tested with:
##
## [from /etc/release:]
## Solaris 8 4/01 s28s_u4wos_08 SPARC
## Copyright 2001 Sun Microsystems, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
## Assembled 01 March 2001
##
## [from `uname -a':]
## SunOS nodename 5.8 Generic_108528-08 sun4u sparc SUNW,Ultra-Enterprise
##
## And gcc version 2.95.3, with the Sun binutils in the SUNWbtool package.
## (the package name may be different in earlier revs of Solaris)
##
## SUNWbtool version: 11.8.0,REV=2000.01.08.18.12
## SUNWhea version: 11.8.0,REV=2000.01.08.18.12
##
## Your mileage may vary, but should be similar.

# Default optimizations.
CFLAGS   = -pthreads -O2 -fomit-frame-pointer -Wall -I$(INCOUT) -DNDEBUG \
           -xc++ -fno-rtti -DHTTPD_OS_NAME=\"Solaris\"  \
           -DHTTPD_DOUBLE_ALIGNMENT \
           -fno-implement-inlines

# Default to the GNU C++ compiler and Solaris binutils.
CXX      = /usr/local/bin/g++
AR       = /usr/ccs/bin/ar
RANLIB   = /usr/ccs/bin/ranlib
PERL     = /usr/bin/perl

# Default libraries needed (assuming use of POSIX threads and BSD sockets)
SYSLIBS   = -lsocket -lnsl -lpthread

# Everything else is POSIXly delicious.
include $(DEPTH)/ports/POSIX

